<%- include('partial/head') %>
</head>
<body class="bg-gray-100 font-sans">
  <%- include('partial/header') %>
  </h1>
  <main class="container mx-auto bg-white shadow-lg rounded-lg p-8 mt-10 max-w-xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl text-gray-800 font-bold text-center mb-6">Programming for Problem Solving</h2>
    <h1 class="text-2xl">Unit 1.0:Introduction to Programming</h1>
    <p>Inyroduction to components of a computer system (disk, memory, processor, where a program is stored and executed, operating system,compilers etc.)</p>
    <p>Idea of Algorithm: Steps to solve logical and numerical problems</p>
    <p>Representation of Algorithm: Flowchat/Pseudo code with exampls</p>
    <p>From algorithms to programs; source code</p>
    <p>Variables(with data types) variables and memory locations</p>
    <p>Syntax and Logical Errors in compilation</p>
    <p>Object and executable code</p>
    <h1 class="text-2xl">Unit 2.0:Operators, Conditional Branching and Loops</h1>
    <p>Arithmetic expressions/arithmetics operators</p>
    <p>Relational operators</p>
    <p>Logical operators</p>
    <p>Biteise operators and precedence</p>
    <p>Writing and evalution of conditionals and consequent branching</p>
    <p>Iteration and loops</p>
    <h1 class="text-2xl">Unit 3.0:Array and String</h1>
    <p>Array declaration & initialization</p>
    <p>Bound checking arrays(1-d,2-d)</p>
    <p>Character arrays and string</p>
    <h1 class="text-2xl">Unit 4.0:Function, Recursion and Pointer</h1>
    <p>Functions (Including using built in Libraries)</p>
    <p>Parameter passing in functions</p>
    <p>Call by value</p>
    <p>Passingarray to function: Recursion,as a different way of solving problems</p>
    <p>Example problems, such as Finding Factorial, Fibonacci series, Ackerman function etc</p>
    <p>Idea of pointers</p>
    <p>Defining pointers</p>
    <p>Use of Pointers in self-referential structures</p>
    <p>Idea of call by reference</p>
    <h1 class="text-2xl">Unit 5.0:User define Data Types and File handling</h1>
    <p>Structure: defining, declaring, initializing; accessing structure members, processing of structures, array of structures, structures within structure and function, type definition</p>
    <p>Union: defination, declaration, accessing union members, initializing union</p>
    <p>Introduction to file handling, file declaration, opening and closing a file, working with text and binary files, I/O operations on file, error handling,rendom access to file</p>
    <h1 class="text-2xl">Unit 6.0:Basic Algorithms</h1>
    <p>Searching</p>
    <p>Basic Sorting Algorithms (Bubble, Insertion and Selection)</p>
    <p>Finding roots of equations</p>
    <p>Notice of order of complexity through example programs (no formal definition required)</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl text-gray-800 font-bold text-center mb-6">Text/Reference Books</h2>
    <h1>1. Programming in ANSI C 4th Ed. E Balagurusamy, McGraw Hill Education India Private Limited, ISBN-978-9339219666, 7th Edition</h1>
    <h1>2. The C Programming Language 2e, W, kernighan / Dennis Ritchie, Pearson Education India, 978-9332549449, 2nd Edition</h1>
  </main>
</body>
</html>